Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||09:38 AM||||some depends on if your willing to do any prep work yourself. Its pretty ez, not rocket science. They can range anywhere from a Maaco cheapy around $200. to upwards of $2,000. Someone who pays someone else generally gets a pretty good job for less that $1,000.<P>oops forgot -its the same paint as on every other car, nothing special for plastic.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boomtastic||08-05-2001||10:48 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hutch84fierose:<BR><B>I heard you need some special paint but I am not to sure.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No special paint needed. I have a 4 page, 237k article in Adobe PDF format that explains (briefly) how to prep and paint plastic automobiles, highlighting the Fiero. If you or anyone wants a copy, you can download it from my web site @ <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.boomtastic.com</A>  in the "Repair" section.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif">   <P>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 08-05-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||4
